WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
Failclosed checks reviewer output
before a merge decision.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.220
Here I am exercising its released
native parser

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.620
with synthetic replies. A well
formed clean review

4
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.700
passes the shape check.

5
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.220
Now the verdict is truncated.

6
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.520
The parser still reports what it
could read,

7
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.160
but marks the schema invalid.

8
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.400
A readable response is not
automatically a usable

9
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:20.880
review.

10
00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.507
A fix verdict with no file finding
is

11
00:00:23.507 --> 00:00:26.767
invalid too. This demonstrates the
parser boundary.

12
00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:30.487
The complete workflow also handles
reviewer execution and

13
00:00:30.487 --> 00:00:32.147
bot threads; it was not run here.

14
00:00:32.707 --> 00:00:34.067
See the source for that integration.
